# ============================================================================
#  LINE COOK COUNTERTOP: KITCHEN-ONLY (.gitignore entries)
# ============================================================================
# The files and folders in here define part of the line cooks kitchen countertop
# This includes everything that should NOT get shipped out of the kitchen (github)
# A good dish is a clean dish. Mess and germs should stay in the kitchen.
#
# Sole source of truth for .gitignore - nothing here is auto-merged from
# elsewhere. Write it by hand:
#   - Everything in .contraband MUST also be listed here (a shady-stash
#     symlink must never end up tracked by git).
#   - Anything in .dishsoap you also want gitignored must be duplicated
#     here too - on purpose, so you actually think about each one.

# Bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Virtual environments (machine-specific, rebuilt with `uv sync`)
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets (also in .contraband)
.env

# Tool caches: ruff, pytest, mypy, hypothesis
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Coverage (pytest-cov)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Packaging output
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter autosaves
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Kept in git on purpose: uv.lock, .python-version, pyproject.toml
